# Unity writes its own files with LF line endings. Left to core.autocrlf (on by default with Git for Windows), git expects CRLF in
# the working copy, and every file Unity rewrites is listed as modified though not a byte of it differs from what is committed:
# hundreds of them after any scene rebuild, hiding the real changes. With these, LF is what the working copy holds.
*.unity      text eol=lf
*.prefab     text eol=lf
*.asset      text eol=lf
*.meta       text eol=lf
*.mat        text eol=lf
*.anim       text eol=lf
*.controller text eol=lf
*.mask       text eol=lf
